# Task Description

As a professional Rust developer, you are tasked to convert an api calling sequence of crate `{crate_name}` into a complete Rust program. The program should match the following requirements:

- The program should call all the apis in api sequence and keep the calling order.
- The program should be syntactically correct and compile without errors.
- The program should read all primitive parameters from stdin.
- The program should only be written in one file with function `main`.
- The program should be suitable for fuzzing.
- All generics without constraints can be replaced with any concrete types.
- No other dependencies should be used except those mentioned in the API documentation.
- Strictly follow all documented safety guidelines when using unsafe blocks to ensure the code remains sound and memory-safe.
- Always include a // SAFETY: comment explaining why the requirements are met.
- Ensure that the input transformation logic is robust and panic-free. Avoid using .unwrap(), .expect(), or direct indexing that could go out of bounds. Instead, use safe pattern matching (if let, match) to handle malformed inputs gracefully.

# Output Format

The output should be in plain text format, given the Rust code directly. No explanations or additional text should be included. No markdown formatting.

